@copilot Update existing PR #20977 directly on its existing head branch. The user approved the following seven readability refinements and the rule clarification. Removing nested ternaries does not mean expanding every single ternary. Preserve the PR's main base and draft state, all behavior, all earlier accepted exclusions, and the other nine refactors. Do not create a separate PR or change other branches.

Clarify the new conditional-expression guidance in docs/contributing/style-guide.md and its corresponding guidance in .github/instructions/java-style.instructions.md and .github/instructions/java-tests.instructions.md. Add this meaning without duplicating verbose prose: "When splitting a nested ternary, retain a simple ternary within a branch when it clearly expresses a two-value choice. Remove only enough nesting to make the decisions easy to follow; do not mechanically expand every ternary into if/else." Retain the existing rule against directly nested ternaries, the exclusion for an inner ternary in a separate method-call argument, and the exception for inline attribute-assertion expected values. Ordinary single ternaries remain appropriate.

Apply precisely these seven replacements in the indicated existing methods. Code snippets are the approved shapes; format them using repository tools. Keep the Long.valueOf call in the Elasticsearch expression, preserve null handling, short-circuiting and evaluation order, and avoid introducing helpers, constants, or other abstractions. Do not rewrite the other refactors merely for uniformity.

1. instrumentation/elasticsearch/elasticsearch-transport-5.0/javaagent/src/test/java/io/opentelemetry/javaagent/instrumentation/elasticsearch/transport/v5_0/Elasticsearch5TransportClientTest.java, assertConfiguredTarget:

```java
Long serverPort;
if (addressList == null) {
  serverPort = getPort() == 9300 ? null : Long.valueOf(getPort());
} else {
  serverPort = sharedPort;
}
```

2. instrumentation-api-incubator/src/test/java/io/opentelemetry/instrumentation/api/incubator/semconv/messaging/MessagingAttributesExtractorTest.java, the test getter's getErrorType:

```java
@Override
public String getErrorType(Map<String, String> request, String response, Throwable error) {
  if ("failure".equals(response)) {
    return response;
  }
  return error == null ? null : error.getClass().getName();
}
```

3. instrumentation/grpc-1.6/testing/src/main/java/io/opentelemetry/instrumentation/grpc/v1_6/AbstractGrpcTest.java, serverErrorType in assertMetrics, not the accepted inline attribute assertion elsewhere:

```java
String serverErrorType;
if (emitPreviewRpcSemconv() && isServerErrorCode(statusCode)) {
  serverErrorType = statusCode.name();
} else {
  serverErrorType =
      emitPreviewRpcSemconv() && status.getCause() != null
          ? status.getCause().getClass().getName()
          : null;
}
```

4. instrumentation/netty/netty-3.8/javaagent/src/test/java/io/opentelemetry/javaagent/instrumentation/netty/v3_8/server/Netty38ServerTest.java, exceptionCaught:

```java
String message;
if (ex.getCause() == null) {
  message = "<no cause>";
} else {
  message = ex.getCause().getMessage() == null ? "<null>" : ex.getCause().getMessage();
}
```

5. instrumentation/rabbitmq-2.7/javaagent/src/test/java/io/opentelemetry/javaagent/instrumentation/rabbitmq/v2_7/RabbitMqTest.java, verifySpan:

```java
String spanName;
if (operation == null) {
  spanName = normalizedResource;
} else {
  spanName = anonymousDestination ? operation : operation + " " + destination;
}

span.hasName(spanName);
```

6. instrumentation/rocketmq/rocketmq-client-4.8/testing/src/main/java/io/opentelemetry/instrumentation/rocketmqclient/v4_8/AbstractRocketMqClientTest.java, expected trace size:

```java
boolean hasBatchCreateSpans = hasBatchCreateSpans();
int size = 2;
if (hasBatchCreateSpans) {
  size = existingCreationContext ? 3 : 4;
}
trace.hasSize(size);
SpanContext spanContext =
    spanNamed(trace, size, "send " + sharedTopic).getSpanContext();
```

7. instrumentation/spring/spring-rabbit-1.1/javaagent/src/test/java/io/opentelemetry/javaagent/instrumentation/spring/rabbit/v1_1/SpringRabbitMqTest.java, errorType in testProducerBatchWithMessageListener:

```java
String errorType = null;
if (fail) {
  errorType =
      testLatestDeps()
          ? "org.springframework.amqp.rabbit.support.ListenerExecutionFailedException"
          : "org.springframework.amqp.rabbit.listener.exception.ListenerExecutionFailedException";
}
```

Leave Spring Rabbit's settlement-operation refactor unchanged. Leave the fully expanded InfluxDB argument-type classification and JDBC configured-target selection unchanged. Also retain the existing compact startup, RPC, Dubbo, ClickHouse, Lettuce, and RMI refactors. Accepted nested ternaries inside attribute assertions and method-call-separated conditional expressions must remain untouched.

Read applicable repository instructions, run the narrowest relevant spotlessApply tasks before focused behavioral validation, and report any limitations in the coding result. Do not alter test expectations, telemetry, configuration, APIs, or the intended nested-ternary policy beyond the clarification above. Keep this update scoped to the seven snippets and their directly related guidance.

@copilot Update existing PR #20977 directly on its existing head branch with these two user-approved readability revisions. Preserve the main base, draft state, all behavior, and all other existing changes. Do not create another PR or update another branch.

In benchmark-overhead/src/test/java/io/opentelemetry/startup/StartupReportTest.java, replace the mutable duration selection in fasterSamples with clearly named candidate durations and one final selection. Rename the method parameter agentAot to aotWithAgentJvmSeconds, normal to normalJvmSeconds, and the selected duration aot to jvmSeconds. Use this shape:

```java
private static List<StartupSample> fasterSamples(double aotWithAgentJvmSeconds) {
  List<StartupSample> samples = new ArrayList<>();
  for (Variant variant : Variant.values()) {
    double normalJvmSeconds = variant.agent() ? 10 : 4;
    double aotJvmSeconds = variant.agent() ? aotWithAgentJvmSeconds : 2;
    double jvmSeconds = variant.aot() ? aotJvmSeconds : normalJvmSeconds;
    samples.add(new StartupSample(variant, 0, 1, true, "ok", 1, normalJvmSeconds, 2));
    samples.add(new StartupSample(variant, 1, 1, false, "ok", 1, jvmSeconds, 2));
    samples.add(new StartupSample(variant, 2, 1, false, "ok", 1, jvmSeconds, 2));
  }
  return samples;
}
```

Preserve the deliberately normal duration for the discarded round-0 sample, including AOT variants. Keep all numeric values and assertions unchanged. Do not introduce new helpers, constants, or abstractions.

Simplify only the conditional-expression guidance added by this PR in the following three files, using the user-approved wording below. In docs/contributing/style-guide.md, replace the current Conditional expressions section with:

```markdown
### Conditional expressions

Avoid directly nested ternaries, even when parenthesized. Use named intermediate values, `if`/`else`, or early returns, keeping simple ternaries where they improve readability.

A ternary inside a separate method-call argument does not count as direct nesting. In tests, nested ternaries may remain inline in attribute-assertion expected values.
```

In .github/instructions/java-style.instructions.md, use that same wording under the existing Conditional expressions bullet, without duplicating the heading. In .github/instructions/java-tests.instructions.md, replace only the new long nested-ternary bullet with:

```markdown
- Nested ternaries are allowed directly in attribute-assertion expected values. Other test code follows the normal conditional-expression rule.
```

Apply normal repository Markdown wrapping and formatting. Leave the surrounding pre-existing test guidance intact, including the following bullet about not extracting ternaries into helpers. Do not add examples, context inventories, or more explanations. The policy is unchanged: no general hasName exception and no new documented exceptions. Leave RmiTest.java untouched, including its restored inline assertion. Leave every other Java refactor and earlier accepted exclusion untouched.

Read applicable repository instructions. Run the narrowest relevant spotlessApply task before focused StartupReportTest validation. Apply the repository Markdown formatter only to the three changed Markdown files if required by its instructions. Report any validation limitations in the coding result.

